-- title:
--   Euler characteristic drops by rd under twisting by I^r
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field, let $\iota : Y \to X$ be a morphism of schemes and let $y : Y \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ be proper. Let $I$ be a quasi-coherent ideal sheaf datum on $X$ which is invertible in the sense that every point of $X$ has a neighbourhood of the form $X.\mathrm{basicOpen}\,f$, for $f$ a section over an affine open $U$, on which $I$ is generated by a single non-zero-divisor; assume the inverse image $I.\mathrm{comap}\,\iota$ on $Y$ is invertible in the same sense. Let $d : \mathbb{N}$, and assume the closed immersion of the subscheme cut out by $I.\mathrm{comap}\,\iota$ followed by $y$ is a finite morphism whose $\mathrm{finrank}$ at every point of $\operatorname{Spec} k$ equals $d$. Let $M$ be an $\mathcal{O}_X$-module which is invertible, i.e. each point of $X$ has an open neighbourhood $U$ on which the pullback of $M$ along $U \hookrightarrow X$ is isomorphic to the unit module; let $r : \mathbb{N}$, and let $\mathcal{W}$ be a cover of $Y$ by two affine opens $U_0, U_1$ with $U_0 \sqcup U_1 = \top$ and $U_0 \sqcap U_1$ affine. Writing, for an $\mathcal{O}_Y$-module $N$, $H^0$ and $H^1$ for the kernel and cokernel of the two-chart Čech differential $\Gamma(N,U_0) \times \Gamma(N,U_1) \to \Gamma(N, U_0 \sqcap U_1)$, $(m_0,m_1) \mapsto m_1|_{U_0 \sqcap U_1} - m_0|_{U_0 \sqcap U_1}$, regarded as $k$-modules via $y$, the asserted identity in $\mathbb{Z}$ is
--   $$\dim_k H^0\bigl(\iota^*((I^r).\mathrm{module} \otimes M)\bigr) - \dim_k H^1\bigl(\iota^*((I^r).\mathrm{module} \otimes M)\bigr) = \dim_k H^0(\iota^* M) - \dim_k H^1(\iota^* M) - r d,$$
--   where $(I^r).\mathrm{module}$ is the kernel of $\mathcal{O}_X \to (\text{pushforward of } \mathcal{O}_{V(I^r)})$ and the dimensions are $k$-ranks coerced to integers.
--
--   This is the additivity of the degree of a line bundle on a proper $k$-scheme under twisting by an effective Cartier divisor, in the negative direction: $\chi(\iota^*(\mathcal{O}_X(-rZ) \otimes M)) = \chi(\iota^* M) - r\deg(Z|_Y)$, with Euler characteristics computed from a two-chart Čech complex. It is the counterpart of the positive-twist statement `eulerChar_sectionsOf_tensor_invModule_eq`, and feeds the multidegree computations for products and iterated twists by several invertible ideal sheaves used on regular models of modular curves.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_Scheme_IdealSheafData_IsInvertible_eulerChar_sectionsOf_pullback_pow_module_tensor_eq_sub_mul.lean

